  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1105 PM CDT WED AUG 5 2026\n\nThis evening, the upper shortwave trough that dipped across the\nSoutheast US should be absorbed back into the main upper trough\nacross North Central and Northeast Conus by Thursday morning.\nAfter that Alabama will be in a benign weak area south of the \nmain broad flat trough and in-between two ridges, one across the \nFour Corners and the other elongated extending eastward off of the\nVA/NC Coast with only minor perturbations traversing the weak \nflow across Central Alabama. This will result in typical summertime\ndiurnally enhanced convection that will be mainly outflow driven.\nBy Monday, the Western Atlantic ridge flattens and retrogrades \nwestward across the Northern Gulf Coast. The only difference will\nbe the slightly better rain chances before this will be in the \neastern half. After this reorientation of the upper ridge, the \nnorthern areas may see a tad more effects from shortwave activity,\nbut not by much.\n\nAs for temperatures, readings do climb up a small amount this\nweekend with overall moisture not changing much. This will result\nin max afternoon heat indices perhaps a few degrees higher in \nspots. However, at this time, guidance does not warrant a heat \nadvisory just yet. Will be monitoring this over the next couple of\ndays if that trend changes.\n\n08",
